  <div class="section-title">Produce</div>
  <ul>
    <li>[ ] Garlic: 1 head (~2.5 oz/70 g)</li>
    <li>[ ] Ginger: 1 medium knob, 3–4 in (2–3 oz/60–85 g)</li>
    <li>[ ] Scallions: 1 large bunch (8–10)</li>
    <li>[ ] Red bell peppers: 2 medium (about 1 lb/450 g)</li>
    <li>[ ] Celery: 4 stalks (about 12 oz/340 g)</li>
    <li>[ ] Cucumber: 1 medium (10–12 oz/280–340 g)</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="section-title">Proteins</div>
  <ul>
    <li>[ ] Boneless skinless chicken thighs: 3 lb (1.36 kg)</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="section-title">Mushrooms</div>
  <ul>
    <li>[ ] Cremini mushrooms: 12 oz (340 g)</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="section-title">Dry goods</div>
  <ul>
    <li>[ ] Dried wheat noodles: 1 lb (454 g)</li>
    <li>[ ] Roasted peanuts, unsalted: 3/4 cup (about 3.5 oz/100 g)</li>
    <li>[ ] Dried red chilies: 0.2 oz (6 g), ~12–15 pods</li>
    <li>[ ] Sichuan peppercorns: 1 tsp (about 0.1 oz/3 g)</li>
    <li>[ ] Granulated sugar: 1/2 cup (3.5 oz/100 g)</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="section-title">Oils, sauces, vinegar</div>
  <ul>
    <li>[ ] Dark soy sauce: buy 5–10 fl oz (150–300 ml)</li>
    <li>[ ] Chinkiang (black) vinegar: buy 8 fl oz (240 ml)</li>
    <li>[ ] Toasted sesame oil: buy 5 fl oz (150 ml)</li>
    <li>[ ] Neutral high-heat oil: 16 fl oz (473 ml)</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="section-title">Optional but nice</div>
  <ul>
    <li>[ ] Oyster sauce: 8 fl oz (240 ml)</li>
    <li>[ ] Star anise: 1–2 pods (about 0.1 oz/3 g)</li>
    <li>[ ] Baking soda: small box (need 1/2 tsp)</li>
    <li>[ ] Toasted sesame seeds: 1–2 tbsp (0.5–1 oz/15–30 g)</li>
    <li>[ ] Low-sodium chicken stock or bouillon: 1 cup (240 ml)</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="notes">
  Notes:
</div>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="section-title">Brand picks & smart substitutions</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Dark soy sauce: Lee Kum Kee Premium Dark; Pearl River Bridge Superior Dark</li>
    <li>Chinkiang vinegar: Hengshun/Gold Plum (Zhenjiang)</li>
    <li>Toasted sesame oil: Kadoya</li>
    <li>Neutral oil: Peanut (LouAna/Hain); or canola/rice bran (Spectrum)</li>
    <li>Dried red chilies: Facing Heaven/Tien Tsin (The Mala Market; 99 Ranch house brands)</li>
    <li>Sichuan peppercorns: The Mala Market; 50Hertz; Penzeys/Frontier Co-op</li>
    <li>Dried wheat noodles: A-Sha, Tseng, or generic “lo mein/Shanghai” dried; fresh: Twin Marquis</li>
    <li>Roasted peanuts: Planters Unsalted dry-roasted; 365/Trader Joe’s unsalted</li>
    <li>Oyster sauce (optional): Lee Kum Kee Premium (with oyster extract); Megachef</li>
  </ul>
  <ul>
    <li>Dark soy swap: 1 tbsp regular soy + 1/2 tsp molasses or dark brown sugar</li>
    <li>Chinkiang swap: rice vinegar + 1/4 tsp balsamic per tbsp (or rice vinegar + pinch sugar)</li>
    <li>Sesame oil swap: mild tahini whisked with a little neutral oil</li>
    <li>Dried chili swap: red pepper flakes (1/2–1 tsp) or fresh Fresno/serrano</li>
    <li>Sichuan peppercorn swap: coarse black pepper + tiny pinch orange zest</li>
    <li>Oyster sauce swap: 2 tsp soy + 1/4 tsp sugar + 1/4 tsp fish sauce (or dab hoisin)</li>
    <li>Peanut swap: cashews or toasted almonds</li>
    <li>Noodle swap: spaghetti (add 1/2 tsp baking soda to boiling water per 8 oz) or fresh udon</li>
    <li>Cremini swap: baby bella or sliced portobello caps</li>
  </ul>
</div>

</body>
</html>

